1
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:04,590
I see.

2
00:00:04,673 --> 00:00:06,860
I just have one question for you.

3
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:10,060
What kind of lunatic
adopts a water monster?

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,297
Well there, don't call her that.

5
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:15,377
She's not a monster, she's
my baby and my familiar.

6
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:18,337
I admit I was frightened of
the creature at first too,

7
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:21,037
but it's actually quite
a docile little thing.

8
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:22,940
Docile monsters do not exist!

9
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:25,637
Or have you forgotten the
chaos we just endured?

10
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:29,014
I have not, but Ralaire's a
total sweetheart, I promise.

11
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,637
Wait just a moment, what is Ray Lair?

12
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:34,077
Don't tell me you named that abomination!

13
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,657
After you and me, of course.

14
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:37,680
Ray plus Claire equals Ray Lair!

15
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:42,017
You would disgrace my name by
bestowing it upon that menace!

16
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:43,397
Oh, stop it, it's cute!

17
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,197
She's like the root of our love.

18
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,597
If that's what you think,

19
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:50,037
then that's all the more reason
to have Professor Torrid kill it!

20
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:51,817
Please don't do that, Miss Claire!

21
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:52,937
Ray Lair's a good girl!

22
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:54,902
She even knows how to do tricks!

23
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:56,270
Sit.

24
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:57,270
Lay down.

25
00:00:58,140 --> 00:00:59,100
Roll over!

26
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:01,320
So smart!

27
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:02,497
What do you mean, smart?

28
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:03,600
It barely moved!

29
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:05,557
That's it, I'm telling the professor!

30
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:06,470
No, wait!

31
00:01:06,553 --> 00:01:07,937
You haven't seen the best part!

32
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:09,300
Alright, girl. Ready?

33
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:10,877
It's go time.

34
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:11,860
Now, undeen!

35
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:24,800
It's me!

36
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:26,037
In miniature!

37
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:29,237
When a water slime is in the
presence of a beautiful lady,

38
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:31,517
it will often assume her form, like so.

39
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:33,200
My, is that really true?

40
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:34,870
Sure!

41
00:01:34,953 --> 00:01:36,200
Kinda sorta halfway true.

42
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:39,617
They actually just mimic the
shape of whatever's nearby.

43
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:43,053
It's a type of camouflage they
use to protect themselves.

44
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:47,204
No harm in Miss Claire believing
the beautiful lady part, though.

45
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:49,340
What a fascinating ability.

46
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,180
I suppose it is rather endearing.

47
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:53,930
Got him!

48
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:56,357
Oh, very well then.

49
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:58,597
I will not have the
creature done away with,

50
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:01,797
but in return you are responsible
for teaching it proper discipline.

51
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:03,357
Thank you very kindly, my queen.

52
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:04,897
It shall be done post-haste.

53
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:06,300
And no sneaking about.

54
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:08,677
You'll reveal its existence to everyone.

55
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:09,590
Okay.

56
00:02:09,673 --> 00:02:12,080
Lastly, the name Ray
Laher simply won't do.

57
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:14,377
You'll need to come up with a new one.

58
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:16,757
Oh, ship sailed on that one, I'm afraid.

59
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,920
Meaning what? Well, um,

60
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:23,777
a familiar never forgets its name, so once
you give it one, there's no going back.

61
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:27,820
This little cutie will forever
be known, Ezreal! I object!

62
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:29,826
With my whole heart and soul!

63
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:57,860
That's the reason How do you know
how to create a world that exists?

64
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:00,937
For a time, you're so familiar
with the thought meaning and right?

65
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:02,608
It's not that you can tell.

66
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:06,257
It's not something you can tell.

67
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:08,277
A thing with your mind.

68
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,417
I don't care.

69
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:10,330
So real.

70
00:03:10,413 --> 00:03:15,937
I love you.

71
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:19,757
I love you. I love you.

72
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:22,057
I love you.

73
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:26,260
I don't know how it's going to start.

74
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:28,660
So let's go.

75
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:30,300
I'm right back.

76
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:33,980
No, I'm not.

77
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:36,540
I'm just one thing.

78
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:38,740
I'm not.

79
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:46,617
Let's go.

80
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:51,700
One more time!

81
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:55,194
I don't want to give up until I forget!

82
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,330
It's fun!

83
00:03:56,413 --> 00:03:57,620
I love you!

84
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:17,777
You were very kind.

85
00:04:17,860 --> 00:04:20,507
What about me, feeling
a little ignored here?

86
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:21,757
Oh, who am I kidding?

87
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:23,605
I adore you in ice-clean mode.

88
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:25,637
That is quite enough out of you!

89
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:27,426
You ladies passed, I take it?

90
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:33,371
Of course, this was just the written exam.

91
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:35,597
They say the practical's what matters.

92
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:36,737
Hope you're ready.

93
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:37,980
For a bit of recap,

94
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:41,357
the Academy Knights are self-governed
organization within the school,

95
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:42,377
like student council,

96
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:43,290
but fancier.

97
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:44,477
It's an elite group.

98
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:47,357
Only those who pass the rigorous
entrance exams are admitted,

99
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:49,499
and the competition is mega fierce.

100
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:52,380
You took the exam as well, Misha?

101
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:56,013
I had no idea you were interested
in joining the Knights.

102
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:58,397
Miss Claire asked me to apply for a spot.

103
00:04:58,480 --> 00:05:00,304
She said Ray needed a guardian.

104
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:02,400
That makes sense.

105
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:07,980
Commoner, I want a rematch.

106
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:11,817
If you fail today's practical
exam, you will leave this academy.

107
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:13,417
Again, I do not want to.

108
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:17,177
And again, I insist you think it
over for more than one second!

109
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:19,025
Fine, if that's what you want.

110
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:22,717
Why don't we compete under the same
terms as last time to keep it simple?

111
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,137
Do you think I'm a fool?

112
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:26,537
You're trying to deceive
me again, you trickster!

113
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:28,800
Oh, shucks, you remembered, huh?

114
00:05:29,420 --> 00:05:32,317
All right, how about we just
agree if I fail, then you win?

115
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:35,459
And if I pass, then I win,
nice and straightforward.

116
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:39,417
Wouldn't it be more straightforward
to say that if I pass, I win?

117
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:41,457
That puts me at too great a disadvantage.

118
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:44,417
We both know you're going
to pass with flying colors.

119
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:46,912
Well, seems you aren't totally oblivious.

120
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:49,637
All right, if you win, then what?

121
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:54,367
You agree to do one thing I say, just
like you did in our previous arrangement.

122
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:57,810
Are you there?

123
00:05:57,893 --> 00:05:58,723
Hey!

124
00:05:58,806 --> 00:05:59,637
You're supposed to stay put.

125
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:02,457
Oh, is this the familiar
I've been hearing about?

126
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:03,599
Oh, it's adorable.

127
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:07,455
If you pass the first test, well done.

128
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:09,857
That's the knight's captain, Lorek.

129
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:14,057
the other guy is his vice
captain now moving on

130
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:17,440
to phase two head on outside
for the practical exam

131
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:31,457
welcome to today's main event recruits
it's time for one-on-one mock battles there

132
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:34,457
are 10 rounds and our survey says the most

133
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:39,220
anticipated are the first battle
Bane Bauer vs. Hugh Bauer.

134
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:43,620
The sixth battle, Rod
Bauer vs. Misha George.

135
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:47,680
And the tenth battle, Claire
Francois vs. Ray Taylor.

136
00:06:55,140 --> 00:06:58,680
This special barrier will reduce
the amount of damage taken.

137
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,560
So no holding back.

138
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:03,682
Fight with all your strength
and no reservations.

139
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:07,420
Now then, will our first
combatants please step forward?

140
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:14,320
Do try and go easy on
me, won't you, Thane?

141
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:15,617
Be safe, Prince Dane.

142
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,500
Be safe, Prince Yu. Prince v.

143
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:20,346
Prince action is a great
way to open the show.

144
00:07:20,780 --> 00:07:21,780
Combatants ready?

145
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:23,050
Begin!

146
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:33,569
Looks like Prince Dane
is on the offensive.

147
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,760
He's an advanced user of win magic.

148
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:39,597
He takes an attribute normally
used for support and manipulates

149
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:43,033
it to boost his strength in
the style of a magic warrior.

150
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:50,657
I know you want to win,
but try not to be reckless.

151
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:53,297
That can lead to mistakes and you wouldn't

152
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:55,497
want to hurt your
precious baby brother now,

153
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:56,410
would you?

154
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,200
Keep talking.

155
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:00,890
Water!

156
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:04,330
Yeah!

157
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:06,997
Prince Yu is so versatile
with his attribute.

158
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:10,256
He's using the water to
deflect Prince Lane's attacks.

159
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:14,540
I think it's time we put
some distance between us.

160
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:20,977
If he tries to get near,
he'll slip on the ice.

161
00:08:21,060 --> 00:08:24,217
That's bad news for a close-range
fighter like Prince Thane.

162
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:27,160
Now then, I believe
it's my turn to counter.

163
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:30,820
An intermediate water magic user,

164
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:33,737
Prince Yu has more than a
few tricks up his sleeve.

165
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:36,526
It's no wonder people
call him the Ice Prince.

166
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:39,510
And go!

167
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:42,080
Prince Thane, look!

168
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:51,217
Prince Thane deflects the icicles with
a wall of wind, and now in charge,

169
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:52,737
head on towards his opponent!

170
00:08:52,820 --> 00:08:54,880
Surely he'll slip on the ice! No!

171
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:57,709
He's compressing the
air and walking on it!

172
00:08:59,100 --> 00:08:59,930
Impressive.

173
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:02,360
Ice filler!

174
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:09,369
Prince Thane is trapped
in a prison of ice!

175
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:12,348
His windwall won't help
him out of this one!

176
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,580
All these shards.

177
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:23,960
I yield the match.

178
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:26,480
The first battle is over.

179
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:29,140
The winner is Prince Thane.

180
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:32,301
You make for a worthy
opponent as always, brother.

181
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:35,345
You do as well, though
I suspect you held back.

182
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:38,228
You use ice and water,
but no healing magic.

183
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:40,717
Prince Thane, you're so gallant.

184
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:43,400
Everybody looks cool in a magic battle.

185
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:48,000
Five battles down, on to the sixth.

186
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:50,271
All right, sick of Misha.

187
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:53,280
Well, here we go.

188
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:57,097
Goodness, she's not very enthused, is she?

189
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,886
Can't say I really blame her.

190
00:09:59,060 --> 00:10:02,766
I mean, who would be excited
about going up against Prince Rod?

191
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:04,320
Don't hold back, Misha.

192
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:06,601
I wish you the very best of luck.

193
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:08,100
You're gonna need it.

194
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,717
Thank you for this
opportunity, Prince Rod.

195
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:13,120
Geez, you don't need to be so polite.

196
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:14,240
We're dueling.

197
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:18,777
Fine, I'll just force you to do
your best if that's what it takes.

198
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:19,740
Come on!

199
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:26,134
Hope you don't mind some extra company.

200
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:29,200
Meet my minions, the flame troops!

201
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:35,180
There are so many! Aw,
they're cute! Attack!

202
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:38,140
The minions have taken the field.

203
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,757
Things look dire for Misha.

204
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,180
How will she respond?

205
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:49,800
Was that sound? Wait, what?

206
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:51,737
The minions have all disappeared!

207
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:53,526
What in the world did she do?

208
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:54,997
That noise!

209
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:57,337
It was like fingernails on a jog board!

210
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:59,655
Commoner, you heard it as well, right?

211
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:02,893
Misha wields her wind magic offensively,

212
00:11:03,060 --> 00:11:06,197
channeling it into a sound
to strike her chosen target.

213
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:08,360
The technique is called siren.

214
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:09,980
Clever trick.

215
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:12,580
Alright, how about this?

216
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:15,390
Attack!

217
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:22,420
And burst!

218
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:26,540
What immense firepower!

219
00:11:26,820 --> 00:11:29,880
I don't see how she can
come back from this. Misha!

220
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:32,370
Amazing!

221
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:34,581
She appears completely unscathed!

222
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,620
Was that another wind magic technique?

223
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:39,190
Yep.

224
00:11:39,273 --> 00:11:40,520
It's called Vacuum Ripture.

225
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:43,357
She creates gaps in the
space around her to shut out

226
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:46,217
heat and insulate herself
from the prince's fire magic.

227
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:49,888
Basically, it's the same principle
that makes a thermos work.

228
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:51,560
Wow, good one.

229
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:54,200
You're tougher than I expected. Not bad.

230
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:57,190
Attack!

231
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:09,480
Prince Rod unleashes a barrage of minions!

232
00:12:10,340 --> 00:12:13,340
One strike after another, classic Rod.

233
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:15,120
Such a show-off.

234
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:18,817
Prince Rod's aptitude for fire
magic is only intermediate,

235
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:21,517
but he has an exceptional
amount of magic power.

236
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:25,297
For a match between students, he
seems to be taking things a bit far.

237
00:12:25,380 --> 00:12:26,210
Agreed.

238
00:12:26,293 --> 00:12:27,280
if he keeps this up.

239
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,840
I yield the match.

240
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:38,640
We have a victor! Misha!

241
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:45,080
Why did she collapse like that?

242
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:46,980
Low oxygen. What?

243
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:51,237
Prince Rod's nonstop attacks
and her continuous use

244
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:53,737
of vacuum rupture depleted
her body of the oxygen.

245
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:55,585
it needs to function properly.

246
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:56,820
To put it simply,

247
00:12:56,940 --> 00:13:00,881
Misha was overwhelmed by the sheer
volume of magic he threw at her.

248
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:03,440
Misha, are you okay?

249
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:06,480
I'll be fine, but thank you.

250
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:11,460
You went too far, brother. Did I?

251
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:14,492
We should take her to the nurse's office.

252
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:32,217
Well, folks, this year's mat exam may be
the most exciting one we've ever seen.

253
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:34,157
And there's still one battle left.

254
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,577
You're going to win this for sure, Ms.

255
00:13:35,660 --> 00:13:36,490
Blair! Yeah!

256
00:13:36,573 --> 00:13:38,497
You're not coming or what you're made of!

257
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:41,404
Looks like we're in for
a pretty good show here.

258
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:43,240
Combatants ready!

259
00:13:44,020 --> 00:13:49,380
The 10th battle is Claire
Francois versus Ray Taylor!

260
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:58,600
Prepare yourself, hooray, Taylor.

261
00:13:58,980 --> 00:14:02,557
When we're done here, I will
personally read you your last rites.

262
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:03,470
Sounds great.

263
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:06,040
You and me duking it out should be fun.

264
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:07,640
Fun, did you say?

265
00:14:08,460 --> 00:14:09,980
Yes, I suppose so.

266
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:13,337
If a humiliating defeat
is your idea of leisure...

267
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:16,880
The day's final battle starts now!

268
00:14:23,220 --> 00:14:24,660
Well, that's odd.

269
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:26,337
Neither of the combatants are moving.

270
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:27,250
Do something!

271
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:29,817
It's not a contest if
you just stand there.

272
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:34,177
Oh, but the view from here is so lovely,
I can't bring myself to look away.

273
00:14:34,260 --> 00:14:36,848
Cease your mockery and
fight me, you cretin!

274
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:37,870
Well, well.

275
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:40,617
Waiting on a little old
me to make the first move?

276
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:41,720
Say no more!

277
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:49,406
Ray has summoned a rock wall,
completely encasing her opponent.

278
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:51,300
Quite the effective barrier.

279
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,580
I'll show you.

280
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:01,220
She broke the rock? No, wait!

281
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:03,225
She appears to have melted it!

282
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:04,520
Whoa, nice one.

283
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:06,037
Takes some real heat to do that.

284
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:08,477
I know the fire attribute
is strong against Earth,

285
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:11,325
but even so, I didn't
realize it could melt it.

286
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:14,308
Well, I guess I'll have
to up my game a bit.

287
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:21,220
No, you don't!

288
00:15:25,380 --> 00:15:27,600
A shield made entirely of fire?

289
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:29,317
Since flames aren't solid,

290
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:32,597
a wall of them isn't usually
effective as a means of defense.

291
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:37,092
But if they're hot enough to melt stone
instantly, that changes everything.

292
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:40,277
Her style of controlling
and expertly manipulating

293
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:44,020
fire is why Miss Claire is
known as the Red Lotus Queen.

294
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:47,677
If you're quite finished,
I believe it's my turn.

295
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:51,700
Now, behold the artistic
magic of a noble! Please!

296
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:53,260
Roar more!

297
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:54,800
Wow, no way.

298
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,293
She's using flamelands?

299
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:57,820
Whoa, is it hot in here?

300
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:01,157
Your magic is a work of art
just like you are, Miss Claire.

301
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,440
Will you shut up?

302
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:06,340
Sorry, can't do that.

303
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,100
Such a fool.

304
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:15,634
I'll melt through this flimsy
wall just like the others.

305
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:19,557
How did you...

306
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:23,497
Looks like it's made up a different
material than the last one was.

307
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:25,992
But what could have forstood that attack?

308
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:27,987
Tungsten carbide, my friend.

309
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:30,137
It's about twice as strong as steel,

310
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:33,279
and its melting point is
over 2,000 degrees Celsius.

311
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:35,597
I've got all this knowledge
from my previous life.

312
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:36,920
Might as well use it.

313
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:41,519
I must admit, unlike your character,
your craft is quite disciplined.

314
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:45,060
And yet, I'm afraid you're
still no match for me!

315
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:49,580
Looks like Claire is using
flamelance once again.

316
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:52,540
But this time she's going
bigger! Much bigger!

317
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:55,020
It's time to put an end to this!

318
00:16:57,460 --> 00:16:59,040
Look at that twerp!

319
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:00,080
It's over.

320
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:04,597
From flamelance into a fireball fuselage!

321
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:06,798
What a remarkable control technique!

322
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:11,900
Rey shot down every one!

323
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:14,378
She's still putting up a good fight!

324
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:18,017
She managed to get every single
one with that little time to react?

325
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:20,400
With no missteps at all. How odd.

326
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:24,080
It's as if she anticipated
all of Claire's moves. Well?

327
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:26,160
Yeah, of course she did.

328
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:30,717
Rey spends every waking moment
thinking about her beloved Miss Claire!

329
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:32,977
Yeah, not even gonna try to deny that one.

330
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:37,320
I've memorized every last lovely
detail of Miss Claire's combat style.

331
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:40,440
Bested by a commoner.

332
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:42,140
Admiring my work?

333
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:43,617
Or are you giving up already?

334
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:44,530
Not a chance!

335
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:46,580
My apologies, Prince Rod.

336
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:52,510
Interesting.

337
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:55,525
It seems she's copying
your fire troop minions.

338
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:56,750
Attack!

339
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:01,171
The wall appears to be holding
against this latest barrage.

340
00:18:03,340 --> 00:18:05,380
I see why she'd want to copy me,

341
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:09,137
but Claire doesn't have the magic
power to keep that up for very long.

342
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:11,455
I don't imagine that will be an issue.

343
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:13,482
If her tactic is what I suspect,

344
00:18:13,860 --> 00:18:18,580
she's seeking to deprive Ray of oxygen,
in which case she will not need long.

345
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:21,040
Ray continues to focus on defense.

346
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:26,470
Aha!

347
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:28,160
Defense becomes offense.

348
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:31,137
If Claire can't escape,
that'll be the match.

349
00:18:31,220 --> 00:18:34,161
Yeah, as if I would fall
for the same trick twice!

350
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:39,356
Now she's busting out the gymnastics!

351
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:42,368
Intelligence and
athleticism in one package.

352
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:43,480
I love herself!

353
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:48,137
I don't know what you're planning to do
from up there, but I can't wait to find out!

354
00:18:48,220 --> 00:18:51,580
Impudent wretch, you're too
cocky for your own good.

355
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:55,980
I never imagined I would deploy
this against a mere commoner.

356
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:58,090
Wait!

357
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:03,920
That's the Francois Family Crest!

358
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:06,100
Magic Ray!

359
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:11,440
Huh? Huh?

360
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:16,860
That was only a warning shot.

361
00:19:17,180 --> 00:19:21,260
As you can see, Magic Ray is far
stronger than my other techniques.

362
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:25,260
So much so that even I can
only wield it so many times.

363
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:27,377
You would be wise to surrender.

364
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:32,397
It's true that I probably can't dodge that
once I see it starting so you yield then,

365
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:33,310
you know?

366
00:19:34,060 --> 00:19:36,980
Sorry, but stubbornness
is my biggest pitfall!

367
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:42,801
That's not good.

368
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:48,306
Honestly of all the spells you could use
you pick that one one more for giggles!

369
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,680
Once was undignified and now?

370
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:56,906
Hey down there, you think
you can make it out?

371
00:19:58,340 --> 00:20:00,897
Yes, and you're going
to be sorry when I do!

372
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:05,777
Just wait, I can easily widen this hole
using magic - It's time to give up, Claire.

373
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:06,690
Prince Thane?

374
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:10,517
But why should I surrender
when I'm still able to fight?

375
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:11,718
Think for a moment.

376
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:14,437
Have you forgotten that
Rey is a dual caster?

377
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:17,700
And yet, she hasn't used
her water magic at all.

378
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:20,857
Even though it would have been much
more effective against your fire.

379
00:20:20,940 --> 00:20:23,900
You've been holding back
the entire battle? Yeah.

380
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:29,437
Mocking me again, you
- Away, sorry ladies,

381
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:33,520
but given the situation I must step
in and call the match to a halt!

382
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:37,337
The winner is Ray Taylor!

383
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:42,737
You're an inspiration to us all!

384
00:20:42,820 --> 00:20:47,617
As before, the results of the exam
will be Posted on the bulletin board!

385
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:49,937
If your name is listed,
then you've made the cut!

386
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:55,320
The newest members of The knights
are Prince Rod, Prince Yu,

387
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:57,109
Prince Dane, the commoner,

388
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:58,780
Misha, and me!

389
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:02,927
Oh, did I forget to tell you how
the practical exam is scored?

390
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:05,847
What counts in your
evaluation is raw talent.

391
00:21:06,280 --> 00:21:09,017
Whether you win or lose has
no bearing on the result.

392
00:21:09,100 --> 00:21:09,940
You're joking.

393
00:21:10,780 --> 00:21:11,610
Congratulations!

394
00:21:11,693 --> 00:21:14,257
I can't wait to see what you
two do when you work together.

395
00:21:14,340 --> 00:21:16,516
Just try not to burn down the school.

396
00:21:18,380 --> 00:21:21,077
So looks like I will.

397
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:22,100
Mmm, fine!

398
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:24,457
But the deal was that
you only get one request.

399
00:21:24,540 --> 00:21:26,246
What do you demand this time?

400
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:28,100
Oh, not much.

401
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:32,300
Just promise me again
that you won't give up.

402
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:36,777
Wait, I don't understand
what you're playing at.

403
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:39,317
That's the exact same
thing you wanted before.

404
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:41,040
It sure is, so go ahead.

405
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:43,264
Swear it again, and we're even.

406
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:45,357
Well, alright.

407
00:21:45,440 --> 00:21:46,734
I suppose that's fine.

408
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:53,240
I hereby swear before God that I,
Claire Francois, will never give up.

409
00:21:53,460 --> 00:21:56,257
No matter what happens,
I will not abandon hope.

410
00:21:56,340 --> 00:21:59,780
And I promise to continue
fighting until the end.

411
00:22:01,660 --> 00:22:04,480
Are you truly certain that's all? Yes!

412
00:22:05,540 --> 00:22:06,370
Hold on.

413
00:22:06,620 --> 00:22:09,679
Why do I feel like there's
something I'm forgetting?

414
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:15,280
What am I to do with this?

415
00:22:25,420 --> 00:22:28,220
Thank you.

416
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:48,917
Not even if I'm not in the place.

417
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,117
I'm not in the place.

418
00:22:50,200 --> 00:22:51,937
Get away, go away.

419
00:22:52,020 --> 00:22:52,850
All the time.

420
00:22:52,933 --> 00:22:54,160
You're ready, you're.

421
00:22:56,400 --> 00:23:03,517
I'm not in the place.

422
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:04,430
I'm in the place.

423
00:23:04,513 --> 00:23:05,480
Thank you.

424
00:23:06,660 --> 00:23:08,980
That's a little bit of a cliche, right?

425
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:11,297
I'm not in the place.

426
00:23:11,380 --> 00:23:14,037
I'm not in the place.

427
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:43,200
Even if you want to say something
like this I want to be like this.
